{"availability":"available","full":"Chemaclass/agnostic-ai","name":"agnostic-ai","description":"One source to rule them all: write agents, skills, rules, and hooks once, then sync them to your AI tools.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":25,"forks":5,"created":"2026-05-03T18:47:55Z","updated":"2026-10-19T22:18:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://agnostic-ai.org","topics":["agentic-ai","agents-md","agnostic-ai","ai-agents","claude","claude-code","cli","codex","copilot","cursor","developer-tools","gemini","golang","mcp"],"demo":"https://agnostic-ai.org/playground/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.683Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.683Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.683Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:40.129Z","stars":21,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.497Z","stars":21,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:43:22.830Z","stars":22,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:03:19.775Z","stars":23,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-11T00:23:09.590Z","stars":23,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:01:40.445Z","stars":25,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.683Z","stars":25,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["agnostic-ai keeps your coding tools working from the same project instructions. Edit one source, then run agnostic-ai sync to write the files Claude Code, Codex, and your other tools read.","Each AI tool reads its instructions from different files. Kept by hand, those files fall out of step. agnostic-ai keeps one source in plain Markdown and YAML inside your repository. It needs no account and no service. See Why agnostic-ai.","Each tool supports a different set of spec kinds. The capability matrix shows which tools get what, and the target reference shows the exact paths. Supported tools include Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Copilot, and Kiro."],"features":["Rules, agents, skills, and commands: instructions in one spec format.","Hooks: checks that run before or after a tool acts. See hooks.","MCP servers: connections to outside services, with credentials read from environment variables. See MCP servers.","Capabilities: what an agent may read, run, or call, mapped to each tool's own names. See capabilities. OpenCode agents with a can or tools list keep project permission limits from opencode.json, including native V2…","Model roles: name a model choice once for every tool. See models."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b8fad77cad5f047c173fc5155e125a2fbb4757124d1639952247a6442089495c","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.764Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.764Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"agnostic-ai keeps your coding tools working from the same project instructions. Edit one source, then run agnostic-ai sync to write the files Claude Code, Codex, and your other tools read.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"It needs no account and no service.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"b8fad77cad5f047c173fc5155e125a2fbb4757124d1639952247a6442089495c","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.764Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-19T22:18:14Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Chemaclass/agnostic-ai/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.765Z","hash":"b8fad77cad5f047c173fc5155e125a2fbb4757124d1639952247a6442089495c","originalBytes":6880,"storedBytes":6880,"truncated":false},"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:19:54.683Z","qualityPriority":false,"enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T16:45:08.024Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v0.78.0","tag":"v0.78.0","publishedAt":"2026-10-03T15:09:43Z","url":"https://github.com/Chemacla